    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 275]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization andNational Policies on 23rd of July, 2024\n\n(Published in the Gazette on May 29, 2024)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 6.00Postage : Rs. 150.002-\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nSAFEGUARD MEASURES (AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Safeguard Measures Act, No. 3 of 2018\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2 : This clause amends section 2 of the Safeguard Measures Act, No. 3 of 2018(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) and the legal effect of this section asamended is to make provisions for the powers, duties and functions of the \u201cDirectorGeneral of Commerce\u201d under the principal enactment to be exercised, performed anddischarged by the \u201cSecretary to the Ministry of the Minister assigned the subject ofInternational Trade\u201d.\n\nClause 3 : This Clause amends the principal enactment and this amendment isconsequential to the amendment made by clause 2\n\nSafeguard Measures (Amendment)1\n\n5\n\nShort title\n\n10\n\n15\n\nL. D.- O. 46/2024\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE SAFEGUARD MEASURESACT, NO. 3 OF 2018\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows: -\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Safeguard Measures(Amendment) Act, No. of 2024.\n\n2. Section 2 of the Safeguard Measures Act, No. 3 of 2018,(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is herebyamended in subsection (1) thereof, by the substitution forthe words \u201cthe Director General of Commerce (hereinafterreferred to as the \u201cDirector General\u201d)\u201d, of the words \u201cSecretaryto the Ministry of the Minister assigned the subject ofInternational Trade (hereinafter referred to as the\u201cSecretary\u201d),\u201d."
