    "url_metadata": "https://documents.gov.lk/view/bills/bl_2024.html",
    "lang": "en",
    "url_pdf": "https://documents.gov.lk/view/bills/2024/8/542-2024_E.pdf",
    "doc_number": "542/2024",
    "chunk_id": "2024-08-06-2024-08-06-542-2024-en-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "0294e652c672fa5204f614e0528325c1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1664,
    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 280]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Hon. Premnath C. Dolawatte, Attorney-at-Law,M.P. for Colombo District on 06th of August, 2024\n\n(Published in the Gazette on July 23, 2024)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 24.00Postage : Rs. 150.00\n\n2-2d\n\n2-\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nWw\n\nws\n\nINTERNATIONAL TRADITIONAL SIHELOGY\n\nto incorporate the International Traditional Sihelogy Council (ITSC)\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nCOUNCIL (ITSC) (INCORPORATION)\n\n1International Traditional Sihelogy Council(ITSC) (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nAN ACT TO INCORPORATE THE INTERNATIONAL TRADITIONALSIHELOGY COUNCIL (ITSC)\n\nWHEREAS a Council named and known as the\u201cInternational Traditional Sihelogy Council (ITSC)\u201d, hasheretofore been established in Sri Lanka for the purpose ofeffectually carrying out its objects and transacting all mattersconnected with the said Council according to the rulesagreed to, by its members:\n\nAND WHEREAS the said Council has heretoforesuccessfully carried out and transacted the several objectsand matters for which it was established and has applied tobe incorporated and it will be for the public advantage togrant such application:\n\nBE it therefore enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows:-\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the International TraditionalSihelogy Council (ITSC) (Incorporation) Act, No. of 2024."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_bills",
    "doc_id": "2024-08-06-2024-08-06-542-2024-en",
    "num": "2024-08-06-542-2024-en",
    "date_str": "2024-08-06",
    "description": "International Traditional Sihelogy Council (ITSC) (Incorporation) - Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://documents.gov.lk/view/bills/bl_2024.html",
    "lang": "en",
    "url_pdf": "https://documents.gov.lk/view/bills/2024/8/542-2024_E.pdf",
    "doc_number": "542/2024",
    "chunk_id": "2024-08-06-2024-08-06-542-2024-en-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ac88f4440aa6318de395790a9bc95295",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1966,
    "chunk_text": "BE it therefore enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows:-\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the International TraditionalSihelogy Council (ITSC) (Incorporation) Act, No. of 2024.\n\nShort Title\n\nPreamble\n\nIncorporationof theInternationalTraditionalSihelogyCouncil\n\n2International Traditional Sihelogy Council(ITSC) (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(2) The body corporate shall be deemed to be a VoluntarySocial Service Organization within the meaning and for thepurpose of the Voluntary Social Services Organizations(Registration and Supervision) Act, No. 31 of 1980 and theprovisions of that Act shall apply to and in relation to themanagement of the affairs of the body corporate.\n\n3. (1) Subject to the provisions of any other written law,the general objects for which the body corporate isconstituted are hereby declared to be-\n\n(a)to establish a degree-awarding institution namedthe International Traditional Sihelogy Institution(ITSI);\n\n(b)to promote traditional Sihela medicine, Sihelanursing. Sihela farming, Sihela martial arts, Sihelaastrology, Sihela exorcism and Sihela dance throughthe members representing all three languages i.e.Sinhala, Tamil and English;\n\n(c) to promote the traditional Sihela medicine amongall Sinhala, Tamil and Muslim communities usingthe three languages i.e. Sinhala, Tamil and English;\n\n(d)to take action to boost foreign exchange earningsfor Sri Lanka by supporting the enhancement ofmental and physical health of tourists through thepromotion of international tourism activities byassisting wellness eco-tourism;\n\n(e)to operate a specific Sihelogy In-patient TreatmentUnit for all diseases;\n\n(f)to establish branches of the Sihelogy Institution inforeign countries:\n\nObjects ofthe bodycorporate\n\n3International Traditional Sihelogy Council(ITSC) (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(g)to conduct educational and social courses andprogrammes in collaboration with foreignuniversities;"
  },
