    "chunk_text": "(8) Any internet service provider, internetintermediary or any other person who is liableto disclose any data or any other informationshall have no civil or criminal liability for the\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n11Online Safety (Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(9) Any person who contravenes theprovisions of subsection (7) commits an offenceand shall on conviction be liable toimprisonment of either description for a termnot exceeding two years, or to a fine notexceeding three hundred thousand rupees orto both such imprisonment and fine.\u201d.\n\n21. Section 39 of the principal enactment is herebyamended as follows: -\n\n(1)in subsection (1) of that section, by the substitutionfor the words \u201cAct shall\u201d, of the words \u201cAct, otherthan any offence committed under section 13, shall\u201d;and\n\n(2)by the addition immediately after subsection (2), ofthe following new subsection: -\n\n\u201c(3) For the purposes of the application ofthe provisions of this Act in relation to anyoffence committed outside the territory of SriLanka, such offence shall be deemed to havebeen committed in Sri Lanka.\u201d.\n\n22. Section 49 of the principal enactment is herebyrepealed and the following section is substituted therefor: -\n\nAmendmentof section 39of theprincipalenactment\n\nReplacementof section 49of theprincipalenactment\n\n12Online Safety (Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n49. (1) The Commission shall, by way ofrules, issue codes of practice applicable tointernet service providers and internetintermediaries, formulated under subsection(2) or (3), in relation to the following matters:-\n\n(a)to address harmful online content andbehaviour including hate speech,incitement to violence,misinformation, disinformation,cyberbullying and harassment andonline sexual exploitation and abuse;\n\n(b)to detect, control and safeguard againstcoordinated inauthentic behaviour andany other misuse of online accounts;\n\n(c)to set operating standards andtransparency reporting of proactiveaction taken to limit harmful content;\n\n(d)to prescribe the types of internetintermediaries;"
