    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 285]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs andConstitutional Reforms on 21st of August, 2024\n\n(Published in the Gazette on January 09, 2024)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 24.00Postage : Rs. 150.00\n\n2-2d\n\n2-\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nWw\n\nws\n\nPENAL CODE (AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Penal Code (Chapter 19)\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2: This clause amends certain sections of the Penal Code (Chapter 19) whichappear in the Schedule to the Bill, and the legal effect of the sections as amended is toincrease the fines imposed in respect of the relevant offences.\n\nPenal Code (Amendment)1\n\n5\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 45/2019\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE PENAL CODE ( CHAPTER 19 )\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:-\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Penal Code (Amendment)Act, No. of 2024.\n\n2. The sections of the Penal Code (Chapter 19) specifiedin Column I of the Schedule hereto, are hereby amended bythe substitution for the words specified in the correspondingentry in column III, of the words specified in thecorresponding entry in Column IV of that Schedule for thepurpose of increasing penalties imposed in respect of theoffences specified in Column II thereof.\n\n3. For the avoidance of doubt, it is hereby declared thatthe provisions of section 2 shall not apply in respect of anoffence referred to in the Schedule, where such offence wascommitted prior to the date of coming into operation of thisAct.\n\n4.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nShort title\n\nAmendmentof certainsections ofChapter 19specified inthe Schedule\n\n10\n\n15\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency\n\nAvoidance ofdoubt"
