    "chunk_text": "(3) Any person who intends to be appointed as a memberof the Commission or who wishes to nominate any othersuitable person, whom he deems it expedient to be appointedas a member of the Commission, may make an applicationto the Constitutional Council expressing his intention to beso appointed or nominating such other person, in suchmanner as may be specified in the rules made under this Act.\n\nCommission for Truth, Unity andReconciliation in Sri Lanka4\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(4) The members of the Commission shall be appointedby the President on the recommendation of theConstitutional Council.\n\n(5) In making its recommendations under subsection (4),the Constitutional Council shall have due regard to theprovisions of subsection (2) and shall take in to account theapplications made under subsection (3).\n\n(6) The Constitutional Council shall recommend threenames from among the members of the Commission to thePresident out of whom the President shall appoint one personas the Chairperson of the Commission.\n\n4. (1) Unless such member vacates office earlier undersubsection (2), every member of the Commission shall holdoffice up to the date of expiration of the term of theCommission in terms of section 9.\n\n(2) The office of a member shall become vacant -\n\n(a)upon the death of such member;\n\n(b)upon such member resigning from such office bywriting addressed to the President;\n\n(c)upon such member being removed from office onany ground specified in subsection (3); or\n\n(d)on the expiration of the term of the Commissionand the consequent expiration of a member\u2019s termof office.\n\n(3) A member of the Commission may be removed fromoffice, by the President with the concurrence of theConstitutional Council, if such person \u2013\n\nTerm ofoffice andremoval ofmembers\n\n5Commission for Truth, Unity andReconciliation in Sri Lanka\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(a)is or becomes a member of Parliament, or a memberof any Provincial Council or any Local Authority;\n\n(b)is adjudged an insolvent by a court of competentjurisdiction;"
